1. Direct Browser Communication

Playwright directly communicates with browsers using native browser protocols.

Example:

Chromium → Chrome DevTools Protocol (CDP)

Selenium uses:

Test Script
   ↓
WebDriver
   ↓
Browser Driver
   ↓
Browser

Extra layers increase:

latency
synchronization issues

Playwright removes many intermediate layers.
-------------------------------------------------------------
2. No External Browser Drivers

Selenium needs:

ChromeDriver
GeckoDriver
EdgeDriver

Playwright has built-in browser management.

Benefits:

less setup
fewer compatibility issues
faster startup

-----------------------------------------------------------
3. Built-In Auto Waiting

Playwright automatically waits for elements before action.

Example:

locator.click();

Internally it waits for:

visible
stable
attached to DOM
enabled

Selenium often requires:

WebDriverWait wait = new WebDriverWait(driver, Duration.ofSeconds(10));

Less manual wait logic → faster + stable execution.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. Faster Parallel Execution

Playwright supports lightweight BrowserContexts.

Instead of launching multiple browsers:

One Browser
   ├── Context 1
   ├── Context 2
   └── Context 3

This reduces:

memory usage
execution time

Selenium Grid setup is heavier.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. Better Modern Web App Handling

Playwright handles:

React
Angular
Vue

more efficiently because it has:

automatic synchronization
network awareness
DOM stability checks
6. Network Interception Built-In

Playwright can:

mock APIs
intercept requests
block resources

without third-party tools.

This speeds up testing.
